    {
      "src": "> [!summary]\n> By CALM, the monotone part of a scheduler (tasks submitted, claims made, \"has it been placed?\") needs no coordination; \"is there room?\" asks about the absence of claims, and does. Omega keeps the scheduling itself coordination-free and puts that question into one atomic step, a commit checked against per-machine sequence numbers, retried on conflict; fine- or coarse-grained checks and incremental or all-or-nothing commits trade retries against guarantees. An escrow of quotas turns the question into an I-confluent one, each scheduler within its own share, and needs coordination only to move quota.",
      "type": "markdown",
      "showWork": false,
      "label": null
    }
